IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 60: RECIPROCAL ENFORCEMENT OF JUDGMENTS (13 rules, with rule 1A): registering in the General
-- Division a judgment of a foreign court under the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959,
-- and obtaining certified copies of a General Division judgment for use abroad.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (the FALSE-kind comment quotes them).
--   NOTHING     the text does not answer on these facts (the NOTHING-kind comment says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: every requirement in the Rules is subject to the Court's
-- discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice; it is not threaded as an input.
-- What follows non-compliance with a Rule is O 3 r 2(4); the functions below that say NOTHING for a "must"
-- not done cite that provision.
--
-- BORROWED FACTS.  The Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959 (the "Act" of this Order) and the
-- Orders extending it to particular countries are not among the sources.  Their sections (4, 5, 13) are named
-- in the inputs and asked as facts; what an extending Order provides is outside the text (rules 3(3), 4, 11, 12).
--
-- TIME.  O 3 r 3(1) says the Interpretation Act does not apply to the calculation of time in these Rules.
-- Whether an act was in time is a comparison with the input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
-- (seam S-T1: roc1's O 3 r 3 computes it, and the merged file wires it).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 60 -- reciprocal enforcement of judgments`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definition of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6973 | 1. In this Order, “Act” means the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959 and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in that Act. [S 91/2023 wef 01/03/2023]
@ref O 60 r 1 "Act" (src:6973)
`o 60 r 1 the Act` MEANS "the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959"

-- "any reference to a section is a reference to a section in that Act".  The text carves out no reference
-- that names another Act expressly; it is silent on one.
-- src:6973 | 1. In this Order, “Act” means the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959 and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in that Act. [S 91/2023 wef 01/03/2023]
@ref O 60 r 1 (src:6973)
GIVEN `the reference is to a section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference names another Act expressly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 1 a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference names another Act expressly`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule does not say what a reference does that names another Act
        IF `the reference is to a section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reference to a section" speaks only of a reference to a section

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1A -- powers under the Act exercisable by Judge or Registrar`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6975 | 1A. The powers conferred on the General Division by the Act may be exercised by a Judge in chambers and the Registrar. [S 91/2023 wef 01/03/2023]
@ref O 60 r 1A (src:6975)
GIVEN person IS A `Decision maker`
      `the Judge sits in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 1A the power conferred on the General Division by the Act may be exercised by the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF person EQUALS `A Judge` AND `the Judge sits in chambers`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF person EQUALS `The Registrar`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be exercised by a Judge in chambers and the Registrar" grants the powers to those two and says nothing of anyone else

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- application for registration`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6977 | 2. An application under section 4 to have a judgment to which Part 1 of the Act applies registered in the General Division must be made by originating application without notice. [S 91/2023 wef 01/03/2023]
@ref O 60 r 2 (src:6977)
GIVEN `the application is under section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment is one to which Part 1 of the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 2 the application for registration is made in the way the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is under section 4` AND `the judgment is one to which Part 1 of the Act applies`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2 speaks of "An application under section 4 to have a judgment to which Part 1 of the Act applies registered"
        IF `the application is made by originating application` AND `the application is made without notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by originating application without notice"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- evidence in support of the application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What the supporting affidavit contains, item by item (rule 3(1)).  Items (c)(ii) is met by either of its two statements
-- ("as the case may require, either ... or ..."); item (d) is required only where interest has become due ("(if any)");
-- the translation in (a) is required only where the judgment is not in English.
DECLARE `o 60 r 3(1) affidavit` HAS
    `o 60 r 3(1)(a) exhibits the judgment or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(a) the judgment is not in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(a) exhibits a translation certified by a notary public or authenticated by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(b) states the names, trades or businesses and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor, so far as known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(i) states that the judgment creditor is entitled to enforce the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(ii) states that at the date of the application the judgment has not been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(ii) states the amount in respect of which the judgment remains unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(iii) states that the judgment can be enforced by the issuance of an enforcement order in the country of the original court and that no ground exists for which its registration may or must be set aside under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(d) interest has become due under the judgment up to the time of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 3(1)(d) specifies the amount of that interest` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6979 | 3. —(1) An application for registration must be supported by an affidavit — ( a )
-- src:6980 | exhibiting the judgment or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy of the judgment, and, where the judgment is not in the English language, a translation of the judgment in that language certified by a notary public or authenticated by affidavit;
-- src:6981 | ( b )
-- src:6982 | stating the names, trades or businesses and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor, so far as known to the deponent;
-- src:6983 | ( c )
-- src:6984 | stating to the best of the information or belief of the deponent — (i)
-- src:6985 | that the judgment creditor is entitled to enforce the judgment;
-- src:6986 | (ii)
-- src:6987 | as the case may require, either that at the date of the application the judgment has not been satisfied, or the amount in respect of which it remains unsatisfied; and
-- src:6988 | (iii)
-- src:6989 | that at the date of the application, the judgment can be enforced by the issuance of an enforcement order in the country of the original court and that no grounds exist for which its registration may or must be set aside under section 5; and
-- src:6990 | ( d )
-- src:6991 | specifying the amount of the interest (if any) which by the law of the country of the original court has become due under the judgment up to the time of registration.
@ref O 60 r 3(1) (src:6979-6991)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 60 r 3(1) affidavit`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 60 r 3(1) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(a) exhibits the judgment or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) exhibiting the judgment or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy of the judgment"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(a) the judgment is not in the English language`)) OR affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(a) exhibits a translation certified by a notary public or authenticated by affidavit` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) a translation of the judgment certified by a notary public or authenticated by affidavit"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(b) states the names, trades or businesses and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor, so far as known` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) the names, trades or businesses and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(i) states that the judgment creditor is entitled to enforce the judgment` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c)(i) that the judgment creditor is entitled to enforce the judgment"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(ii) states that at the date of the application the judgment has not been satisfied` OR affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(ii) states the amount in respect of which the judgment remains unsatisfied` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c)(ii) either that at the date of the application the judgment has not been satisfied, or the amount in respect of which it remains unsatisfied"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(c)(iii) states that the judgment can be enforced by the issuance of an enforcement order in the country of the original court and that no ground exists for which its registration may or must be set aside under section 5` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c)(iii) that at the date of the application the judgment can be enforced by the issuance of an enforcement order in the country of the original court and that no grounds exist for which its registration may or must be set aside under section 5"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(d) interest has become due under the judgment up to the time of registration`)) OR affidavit's `o 60 r 3(1)(d) specifies the amount of that interest` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d) the amount of the interest which by the law of the country of the original court has become due under the judgment up to the time of registration"))

-- src:6979 | 3. —(1) An application for registration must be supported by an affidavit — ( a )
-- src:6980 | exhibiting the judgment or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy of the judgment, and, where the judgment is not in the English language, a translation of the judgment in that language certified by a notary public or authenticated by affidavit;
-- src:6981 | ( b )
-- src:6982 | stating the names, trades or businesses and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor, so far as known to the deponent;
-- src:6983 | ( c )
-- src:6984 | stating to the best of the information or belief of the deponent — (i)
-- src:6985 | that the judgment creditor is entitled to enforce the judgment;
-- src:6986 | (ii)
-- src:6987 | as the case may require, either that at the date of the application the judgment has not been satisfied, or the amount in respect of which it remains unsatisfied; and
-- src:6988 | (iii)
-- src:6989 | that at the date of the application, the judgment can be enforced by the issuance of an enforcement order in the country of the original court and that no grounds exist for which its registration may or must be set aside under section 5; and
-- src:6990 | ( d )
-- src:6991 | specifying the amount of the interest (if any) which by the law of the country of the original court has become due under the judgment up to the time of registration.
@ref O 60 r 3(1) (src:6979-6991)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 60 r 3(1) affidavit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 3(1) the affidavit supporting the application states what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 60 r 3(1) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` affidavit) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be supported by an affidavit"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE

-- Rule 3(2): "Where a judgment ... is in respect of different matters, and some, but not all, ... could properly
-- have been registered", the affidavit "must state the provisions in respect of which the judgment is sought to be registered".
-- src:6992 | (2) Where a judgment sought to be registered under the Act is in respect of different matters, and some, but not all, of the provisions of the judgment are such that if those provisions had been contained in separate judgments, those judgments could properly have been registered, the affidavit must state the provisions in respect of which the judgment is sought to be registered.
@ref O 60 r 3(2) (src:6992)
GIVEN `the judgment is in respect of different matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some but not all of its provisions could properly have been registered if contained in separate judgments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 3(2) the duty to state the provisions arises` MEANS
    IF `the judgment is in respect of different matters` AND `some but not all of its provisions could properly have been registered if contained in separate judgments`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a judgment sought to be registered under the Act is in respect of different matters, and some, but not all, of the provisions of the judgment are such that if those provisions had been contained in separate judgments, those judgments could properly have been registered"

-- src:6992 | (2) Where a judgment sought to be registered under the Act is in respect of different matters, and some, but not all, of the provisions of the judgment are such that if those provisions had been contained in separate judgments, those judgments could properly have been registered, the affidavit must state the provisions in respect of which the judgment is sought to be registered.
@ref O 60 r 3(2) (src:6992)
GIVEN `the judgment is in respect of different matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some but not all of its provisions could properly have been registered if contained in separate judgments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the provisions in respect of which the judgment is sought to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 3(2) the affidavit states the provisions in respect of which registration is sought` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 60 r 3(2) the duty to state the provisions arises` `the judgment is in respect of different matters` `some but not all of its provisions could properly have been registered if contained in separate judgments` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 60 r 3(2) the duty to state the provisions arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF `the affidavit states the provisions in respect of which the judgment is sought to be registered`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must state"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- Rule 3(3): the other evidence depends on "the Order under the Act extending that Act to that country", which is
