@ref O 60 r 3(3) (src:6993)
GIVEN `the affidavit is accompanied by the other evidence the extending Order requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 3(3) the affidavit is accompanied by the other evidence the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit is accompanied by the other evidence the extending Order requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what evidence is "required having regard to the provisions of the Order under the Act extending that Act to that country" is in that Order, and a bare "must be accompanied"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

