§§ `Rule 5 -- order for registration`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 60 r 5(1) the form of the order giving permission to register` MEANS "88"

-- src:6997 | 5. —(1) An order in Form 88 giving permission to register a judgment must be drawn up by, or on behalf of, the judgment creditor and served on the judgment debtor. (2) Every such order must state the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration and must contain a notification that an enforcement order to enforce the judgment will not be issued until after the expiration of that period.
@ref O 60 r 5(1) (src:6997)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 88` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the judgment creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is served on the judgment debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 5(1) the order giving permission to register is drawn up and served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 88` AND `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the judgment creditor` AND `the order is served on the judgment debtor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be drawn up by, or on behalf of, the judgment creditor and served"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- src:6997 | 5. —(1) An order in Form 88 giving permission to register a judgment must be drawn up by, or on behalf of, the judgment creditor and served on the judgment debtor. (2) Every such order must state the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration and must contain a notification that an enforcement order to enforce the judgment will not be issued until after the expiration of that period.
@ref O 60 r 5(2) (src:6997)
GIVEN `the order states the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order contains a notification that an enforcement order will not be issued until after the expiration of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 5(2) the order states the period and contains the notification` MEANS
    IF `the order states the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration` AND `the order contains a notification that an enforcement order will not be issued until after the expiration of that period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "Every such order must state ... and must contain"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

