§§ `Rule 7 -- notice of registration`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7003 | 7. —(1) Notice of the registration of a judgment must be served on the judgment debtor and, subject to paragraph (2), must be served personally unless the Court otherwise orders. (2) Service of such a notice out of Singapore is permissible without permission, and Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply in relation to such a notice as they apply in relation to an originating claim.
@ref O 60 r 7(1) (src:7003)
GIVEN `the notice is served on the judgment debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered that it be served otherwise than personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served in the way the Court ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 7(1) the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notice is served out of Singapore`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): personal service is "subject to paragraph (2)", and paragraph (2) applies Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8, which are in another part
        IF `the notice is served on the judgment debtor` AND (`the notice is served personally` OR (`the Court has ordered that it be served otherwise than personally` AND `it is served in the way the Court ordered`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be served on the judgment debtor and ... personally unless the Court otherwise orders"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- src:7003 | 7. —(1) Notice of the registration of a judgment must be served on the judgment debtor and, subject to paragraph (2), must be served personally unless the Court otherwise orders. (2) Service of such a notice out of Singapore is permissible without permission, and Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply in relation to such a notice as they apply in relation to an originating claim.
@ref O 60 r 7(2) (src:7003)
GIVEN `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
