-- src:7003 | 7. —(1) Notice of the registration of a judgment must be served on the judgment debtor and, subject to paragraph (2), must be served personally unless the Court otherwise orders. (2) Service of such a notice out of Singapore is permissible without permission, and Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply in relation to such a notice as they apply in relation to an originating claim.
@ref O 60 r 7(2) (src:7003)
GIVEN `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rule number of Order 8` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 7(2) a rule of Order 8 applies to the notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice is served out of Singapore` AND elem `rule number of Order 8` (LIST
        "2",
        "3",
        "7",
        "8")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8" are named, and only for service out of Singapore; the paragraph says nothing of other rules

DECLARE `o 60 r 7(3) notice of registration` HAS
    `o 60 r 7(3)(a) states full particulars of the judgment registered and the order for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 7(3)(b) states the name and address of the judgment creditor or of the judgment creditor's solicitor on whom any summons issued by the judgment debtor may be served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 7(3)(c) states the right of the judgment debtor to apply to have the registration set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 7(3)(d) states the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7004 | (3) The notice of registration must state — ( a )
-- src:7005 | full particulars of the judgment registered and the order for registration;
-- src:7006 | ( b )
-- src:7007 | the name and address of the judgment creditor or of the judgment creditor’s solicitor on whom, and at which, any summons issued by the judgment debtor may be served;
-- src:7008 | ( c )
-- src:7009 | the right of the judgment debtor to apply to have the registration set aside; and
-- src:7010 | ( d )
-- src:7011 | the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made.
@ref O 60 r 7(3) (src:7004-7011)
GIVEN notice IS A `o 60 r 7(3) notice of registration`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 60 r 7(3) the matters the notice has not yet stated` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF notice's `o 60 r 7(3)(a) states full particulars of the judgment registered and the order for registration` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) full particulars of the judgment registered and the order for registration"),
        (IF notice's `o 60 r 7(3)(b) states the name and address of the judgment creditor or of the judgment creditor's solicitor on whom any summons issued by the judgment debtor may be served` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) the name and address of the judgment creditor or of the judgment creditor's solicitor on whom, and at which, any summons issued by the judgment debtor may be served"),
        (IF notice's `o 60 r 7(3)(c) states the right of the judgment debtor to apply to have the registration set aside` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c) the right of the judgment debtor to apply to have the registration set aside"),
        (IF notice's `o 60 r 7(3)(d) states the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d) the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made"))

-- src:7004 | (3) The notice of registration must state — ( a )
-- src:7005 | full particulars of the judgment registered and the order for registration;
-- src:7006 | ( b )
-- src:7007 | the name and address of the judgment creditor or of the judgment creditor’s solicitor on whom, and at which, any summons issued by the judgment debtor may be served;
-- src:7008 | ( c )
-- src:7009 | the right of the judgment debtor to apply to have the registration set aside; and
-- src:7010 | ( d )
-- src:7011 | the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made.
@ref O 60 r 7(3) (src:7004-7011)
GIVEN notice IS A `o 60 r 7(3) notice of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 7(3) the notice of registration states what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 60 r 7(3) the matters the notice has not yet stated` notice) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must state"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 8 -- endorsement of service`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7013 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served; and, if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court. (2) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 60 r 8(1) (src:7013)
`o 60 r 8(1) the period for endorsing the notice` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- The 3 days run to the last day that O 3 r 3 counts (O 3 r 3(3): the period begins immediately after the date of
-- service; r 3(6): being 6 days or less it excludes non-court days).  The Court may allow a longer period "in
-- special circumstances"; its last day, if it has allowed one, replaces the 3-day last day when later.
-- src:7013 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served; and, if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court. (2) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 60 r 8(1) (src:7013)
GIVEN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 60 r 8(1) the last day for endorsing the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    WHEN JUST longer THEN IF longer AT LEAST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN longer ELSE `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

-- src:7013 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served; and, if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court. (2) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 60 r 8(1) (src:7013)
GIVEN `the date the notice was endorsed, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the notice was endorsed, if it was`
    WHEN JUST endorsed THEN
        IF endorsed AT MOST `o 60 r 8(1) the last day for endorsing the notice` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date being asked about` AT MOST `o 60 r 8(1) the last day for endorsing the notice` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances, if it has`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the notice is not yet endorsed and the time for endorsing it has not yet run out
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow"

-- src:7013 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served; and, if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court. (2) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 60 r 8(1) (src:7013)
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 8(1) the Court may allow a longer period for endorsing the notice` MEANS
    IF `there are special circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court may allow a longer period "in special circumstances" and the paragraph says nothing of other cases

DECLARE `o 60 r 8(1) endorsement` HAS
    `o 60 r 8(1) made by the person who served the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 8(1) states the day of the week on which it was served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 8(1) states the date on which it was served` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7013 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served; and, if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court. (2) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 60 r 8(1) (src:7013)
GIVEN endorsement IS A `o 60 r 8(1) endorsement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 8(1) the endorsement is what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF    endorsement's `o 60 r 8(1) made by the person who served the notice`
      AND endorsement's `o 60 r 8(1) states the day of the week on which it was served`
      AND endorsement's `o 60 r 8(1) states the date on which it was served`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the person who served the notice (named in the text) must endorse it.  The longer
-- period the Court may allow is not modelled in the rule (it is in `o 60 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time`).
DECLARE `o 60 r 8(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 60 r 8(1) the person who served the notice`

DECLARE `o 60 r 8(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 60 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service`

`o 60 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `o 60 r 8(1) the person who served the notice`
    MUST `o 60 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 60 r 8(1) the person who served the notice` BECAUSE "the notice was not endorsed within 3 days after its service (O 60 r 8(1))"

#TRACE `o 60 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 60 r 8(1) the person who served the notice` DOES `o 60 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service` AT 2
#TRACE `o 60 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 60 r 8(1) the person who served the notice` DOES `o 60 r 8(1) endorse the notice with the day of the week and date of service` AT 3
#TRACE `o 60 r 8(1) the duty to endorse the notice` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 4

-- "if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an
-- enforcement order ... without the permission of the Court."
-- src:7013 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served; and, if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court. (2) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 60 r 8(1) (src:7013)
GIVEN `the answer on whether the notice was endorsed in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 8(1) the judgment creditor may apply for an enforcement order without the permission of the Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer on whether the notice was endorsed in time`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar does not arise, and a bar that does not arise grants no permission; QA: NOTHING (a lifted bar grants nothing) / other: JUST TRUE (the exception permits it)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the notice was endorsed in time is not yet answered

-- src:7013 | 8. —(1) Within 3 days after service of the notice of registration or within such longer period as the Court may, in special circumstances, allow, the notice or a copy of the notice must be endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date on which it was served; and, if the notice is not so endorsed within the abovementioned period, the judgment creditor may not apply for an enforcement order to enforce the judgment to which the notice relates without the permission of the Court. (2) Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date on which the notice was endorsed under this Rule.
@ref O 60 r 8(2) (src:7013)
GIVEN `the affidavit of service states the date on which the notice was endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 8(2) the affidavit of service states the date of endorsement` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit of service states the date on which the notice was endorsed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "Every affidavit of service of any such notice must state the date"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

