§§ `Rule 9 -- application to set aside registration`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7015 | 9. —(1) An application to set aside the registration of a judgment must be made by summons supported by an affidavit. (2) The Court hearing such application may order any issue between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor to be tried in any manner in which an issue in an action may be ordered to be tried.
@ref O 60 r 9(1) (src:7015)
GIVEN document IS A `Document kind`
      `the application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 9(1) the application to set aside the registration is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS Summons AND `the application is supported by an affidavit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by summons supported by an affidavit"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- src:7015 | 9. —(1) An application to set aside the registration of a judgment must be made by summons supported by an affidavit. (2) The Court hearing such application may order any issue between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor to be tried in any manner in which an issue in an action may be ordered to be tried.
@ref O 60 r 9(2) (src:7015)
GIVEN `the Court is hearing an application to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue is between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 9(2) the Court may order the issue to be tried as an issue in an action is tried` MEANS
    IF `the Court is hearing an application to set aside the registration` AND `the issue is between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "The Court hearing such application" over "any issue between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor" and says nothing of any other

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 10 -- issuance of enforcement order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "(1) An enforcement order must not be issued to enforce a judgment registered under the Act until after the
-- expiration of the period ... specified in the order for registration ... or (if that period has been extended by
-- the Court) until after the expiration of that period as so extended."  The "until" bar is its own yes/no (ruling
-- of 2026-11-05 (d)): JUST TRUE before the expiry, JUST FALSE after it.  Nothing here says the order MAY be issued after it.
-- src:7018 | 10. —(1) An enforcement order must not be issued to enforce a judgment registered under the Act until after the expiration of the period which, in accordance with Rule 5(2), is specified in the order for registration as the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration or (if that period has been extended by the Court) until after the expiration of that period as so extended. [S 91/2023 wef 01/03/2023]
@ref O 60 r 10(1) (src:7018)
GIVEN `the judgment is registered under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the specified period expires, as extended by the Court if it was` IS A DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 10(1) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the specified period has not expired` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the judgment is registered under the Act`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to enforce a judgment registered under the Act"
        IF `the date being asked about` AT MOST `the date the specified period expires, as extended by the Court if it was`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until after the expiration of the period"

-- "(2) If an application is made to set aside the registration of a judgment, an enforcement order ... must not be
-- issued until after such application is finally determined."
-- src:7019 | (2) If an application is made to set aside the registration of a judgment, an enforcement order to enforce the judgment must not be issued until after such application is finally determined.
@ref O 60 r 10(2) (src:7019)
GIVEN `an application is made to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that application has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 10(2) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the application to set aside is not finally determined` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an application is made to set aside the registration`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application is made to set aside the registration of a judgment"
        IF NOT (`that application has been finally determined`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until after such application is finally determined"

-- src:7020 | (3) Any party wishing to apply for an enforcement order to enforce a judgment registered under the Act must produce to the Court an affidavit of service of the notice of registration of the judgment and any order made by the Court in relation to the judgment. [S 91/2023 wef 01/03/2023]
@ref O 60 r 10(3) (src:7020)
GIVEN `the party produces to the Court an affidavit of service of the notice of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an order made by the Court in relation to the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party produces that order to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 10(3) the party applying for an enforcement order has produced what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the party produces to the Court an affidavit of service of the notice of registration` AND ((NOT (`there is an order made by the Court in relation to the judgment`)) OR `the party produces that order to the Court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must produce to the Court an affidavit of service ... and any order made by the Court"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- The two "until" bars as prohibitions on a trace.  The text names no one who bears them ("an enforcement order
-- must not be issued"), so the party below is a PLACEHOLDER for whoever issues the order, not an actor the text
-- names; no seat is written for it.  The trace's time unit is a day.
DECLARE `o 60 r 10 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 60 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order`

DECLARE `o 60 r 10 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 60 r 10 issue the enforcement order`

GIVEN `days from the day asked about to the day the specified period expires` IS A NUMBER
`o 60 r 10(1) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 60 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order`
    SHANT `o 60 r 10 issue the enforcement order`
    WITHIN `days from the day asked about to the day the specified period expires`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 60 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` BECAUSE "an enforcement order was issued before the expiration of the specified period (O 60 r 10(1))"

#TRACE `o 60 r 10(1) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 60 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` DOES `o 60 r 10 issue the enforcement order` AT 4
#TRACE `o 60 r 10(1) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order` 10 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 11

GIVEN `days until the application to set aside is finally determined` IS A NUMBER
`o 60 r 10(2) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order while the application is undetermined` MEANS
    PARTY `o 60 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order`
    SHANT `o 60 r 10 issue the enforcement order`
    WITHIN `days until the application to set aside is finally determined`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 60 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` BECAUSE "an enforcement order was issued before the application to set aside was finally determined (O 60 r 10(2))"

#TRACE `o 60 r 10(2) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order while the application is undetermined` 6 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 60 r 10 whoever issues the enforcement order` DOES `o 60 r 10 issue the enforcement order` AT 5
#TRACE `o 60 r 10(2) the prohibition on issuing the enforcement order while the application is undetermined` 6 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 7

