@ref O 60 r 13(2) (src:7026-7037)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 60 r 13(2) affidavit`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 60 r 13(2) the matters the affidavit has not yet covered` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(a) gives particulars of the proceedings in which the judgment was obtained` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) particulars of the proceedings in which the judgment was obtained"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(b) annexes a copy of the originating claim or originating application` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) annexed: a copy of the originating claim or originating application by which the proceedings were begun"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(b) annexes the evidence of service on the defendant or a notice of intention to contest or not contest by the defendant` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) annexed: the evidence of service of the originating claim or originating application on, or a notice of intention to contest or not contest by, the defendant"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(b) there are pleadings`)) OR affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(b) annexes copies of the pleadings` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) annexed: copies of the pleadings"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(b) annexes a statement of the grounds on which the judgment was based` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) annexed: a statement of the grounds on which the judgment was based"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(c) states whether the defendant did or did not object to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c) whether the defendant did or did not object to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore"),
        (IF (NOT (affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(c) the defendant objected`)) OR affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(c) states on what grounds the defendant objected` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c) on what grounds the defendant objected"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(d) shows that the judgment is not subject to any stay of enforcement` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d) that the judgment is not subject to any stay of enforcement"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(e) states that the time for appealing has expired or the date on which it will expire` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(e) that the time for appealing has expired or the date on which it will expire"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(e) states whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(e) whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 60 r 13(2)(f) states the rate at which the judgment carries interest` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(f) the rate at which the judgment carries interest"))

-- src:7026 | 13. —(1) An application under section 13 for certified copies of the pleadings, order of court and written grounds of decision (if any) entered in the General Division must be made by summons without notice to the Registrar supported by an affidavit. (2) The affidavit in support of the application under section 13 must — ( a )
-- src:7027 | give particulars of the proceedings in which the judgment was obtained;
-- src:7028 | ( b )
-- src:7029 | have annexed to it a copy of the originating claim or originating application by which the proceedings were begun, the evidence of service of the originating claim or originating application (as the case may be) on, or a notice of intention to contest or not contest by, the defendant, copies of the pleadings (if any) and a statement of the grounds on which the judgment was based;
-- src:7030 | ( c )
-- src:7031 | state whether the defendant did or did not object to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore and, if so, on what grounds;
-- src:7032 | ( d )
-- src:7033 | show that the judgment is not subject to any stay of enforcement;
-- src:7034 | ( e )
-- src:7035 | state that the time for appealing has expired or (as the case may be) the date on which it will expire and in either case whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered; and
-- src:7036 | ( f )
-- src:7037 | state the rate at which the judgment carries interest.
@ref O 60 r 13(2) (src:7026-7037)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 60 r 13(2) affidavit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 60 r 13(2) the affidavit supporting the application covers what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 60 r 13(2) the matters the affidavit has not yet covered` affidavit) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- Rule 13(3): the copies and the Registrar's certificate.  An official's act; the person who receives the copies
-- checks them against the Rule.  Items (b) and (c) of the certificate are required "(if any)" objections or pleadings.
DECLARE `o 60 r 13(3) certified copies and certificate` HAS
    `o 60 r 13(3) the copies are sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3) a copy of the originating claim or originating application is annexed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3) accompanied by a certificate in Form 90 signed by the Registrar certifying that the judgment is a true copy of a judgment obtained in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(a) states the manner in which the originating claim or originating application was served or that the defendant filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(b) objections were made to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(b) states what objections were made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(c) pleadings were served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(c) states what pleadings were served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(d) states the grounds on which the judgment was based` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(e) states that the time for appealing has expired or the date on which it will expire` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(f) states whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(g) states such other particulars as may be necessary to give to the court in the foreign country in which it is sought to enforce the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 60 r 13(3)(h) states the rate at which the judgment carries interest` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7038 | (3) The certified copies of the pleadings, order of court and written grounds of decision (if any) must be sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court, must have a copy of the originating claim or originating application by which the proceedings were begun annexed to it, and must be accompanied by a certificate in Form 90 signed by the Registrar certifying that the judgment is a true copy of a judgment obtained in the General Division and stating — ( a )
-- src:7039 | the manner in which the originating claim or originating application was served on the defendant or that the defendant filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest;
-- src:7040 | ( b )
-- src:7041 | what objections (if any) were made to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore;
-- src:7042 | ( c )
-- src:7043 | what pleadings (if any) were served;
-- src:7044 | ( d )
-- src:7045 | the grounds on which the judgment was based;
-- src:7046 | ( e )
-- src:7047 | that the time for appealing has expired or (as the case may be) the date on which it will expire;
-- src:7048 | ( f )
-- src:7049 | whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered;
-- src:7050 | ( g )
-- src:7051 | such other particulars as may be necessary to give to the court in the foreign country in which it is sought to enforce the judgment; and
-- src:7052 | ( h )
-- src:7053 | the rate at which the judgment carries interest. [S 91/2023 wef 01/03/2023]
@ref O 60 r 13(3) (src:7038-7053)
GIVEN copies IS A `o 60 r 13(3) certified copies and certificate`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 60 r 13(3) the matters the copies and certificate have not yet satisfied` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3) the copies are sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the certified copies sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3) a copy of the originating claim or originating application is annexed` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "a copy of the originating claim or originating application by which the proceedings were begun annexed"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3) accompanied by a certificate in Form 90 signed by the Registrar certifying that the judgment is a true copy of a judgment obtained in the General Division` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "accompanied by a certificate in Form 90 signed by the Registrar certifying that the judgment is a true copy of a judgment obtained in the General Division"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(a) states the manner in which the originating claim or originating application was served or that the defendant filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) the manner in which the originating claim or originating application was served on the defendant or that the defendant filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest"),
        (IF (NOT (copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(b) objections were made to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore`)) OR copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(b) states what objections were made` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) what objections were made to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore"),
        (IF (NOT (copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(c) pleadings were served`)) OR copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(c) states what pleadings were served` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c) what pleadings were served"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(d) states the grounds on which the judgment was based` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d) the grounds on which the judgment was based"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(e) states that the time for appealing has expired or the date on which it will expire` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(e) that the time for appealing has expired or the date on which it will expire"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(f) states whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(f) whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(g) states such other particulars as may be necessary to give to the court in the foreign country in which it is sought to enforce the judgment` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(g) such other particulars as may be necessary to give to the court in the foreign country in which it is sought to enforce the judgment"),
        (IF copies's `o 60 r 13(3)(h) states the rate at which the judgment carries interest` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(h) the rate at which the judgment carries interest"))

